  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Dogwash Perle and Co, in Mouans-Sartoux, in the Grasse-Cannes area, offers a self-service dog washing station. Dogs up to 80 kg are accepted there, which covers most sizes, including large breeds. The place opened in early 2026, run by Baptiste Paladino, in the presence of local officials, with an interest-free loan of €8,000 via Initiative Terre d'Azur — confirmed by several sources (France 3 Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur, municipal communications, the business's own website).</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The products used are an aloe vera shampoo and a strawberry-scented conditioner. In addition to the self-service wash, classic grooming is also available by appointment, along with a "dog taxi" pick-up service for owners who'd rather have their dog picked up. Advertised opening hours are 7 days a week from 9am to 7pm (to be reconfirmed out of season). This information is cross-checked between the business's official website and the local directory mouanssartouxgo.fr, giving a medium-to-high confidence level. Prices for the wash itself are not disclosed publicly — a single source mentions €2 for park access when not using the machine, to confirm. Better to call or check on site.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the 80 kg threshold covers a wide range, but if your dog is right at the upper limit, a call ahead to confirm the tub size avoids any bad surprises.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Mouans-Sartoux, between Grasse and Cannes, gives quick access both to the perfumeries of Grasse and to the Cannes coastline.</p>
